      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В чем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In what?' Vika asks this with a single word meaning 'than', using rising intonation to turn it into a quick question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "В том, что они имеют.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In what they have.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'that' with 'to have'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это правда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That is true.' Notice how 'this' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'honestly'.",
